@startuml 13-inspect-sequence
skinparam backgroundColor #FFFFFF
title PortCloak — Inspect a Snapshot (tiered, lazy)

actor User
participant "Wails UI" as UI
participant "SnapshotInspector" as INS
participant "IndexStore\n(SQLite, ephemeral)" as IX
participant "BlobStore\n(storage backend)" as S
participant "CryptoVault" as CV
participant "IntegrityService" as IG

== Tier 0 — listing (no keys required) ==
User -> UI : Open Snapshots library
UI -> INS : List(storage backends)
INS -> S : List(prefix) + Get(<id>.manifest.json)
S --> INS : non-secret sidecars
INS --> UI : rows: realm, date, source,\ncounts, completeness badge
note right of INS
  Sidecar manifests carry NO secrets,
  so browsing the library needs no
  decryption key at all.
end note

== Tier 1 — snapshot detail (decrypt manifest only) ==
User -> UI : Open a snapshot
UI -> INS : Describe(snapshotID)
INS -> S : Get(.pck) [resumable]
INS -> CV : Decrypt (if encrypted)
INS -> IG : Verify integrity tree
IG --> INS : OK / mismatch(warn)
INS -> INS : stream-parse envelope + manifest.json
INS -> IX : create session-scoped SQLite index
INS --> UI : realm settings, keys (KIDs),\nclients, IdPs, LDAP, flows,\nsecret ledger, external deps,\ncompleteness

== Tier 2 — browse users & entities (build index once) ==
User -> UI : Open "Users" tab / search
UI -> INS : QueryUsers(snapshotID, filter, page)
alt index already built this session
  IX --> INS : page of users
else build once per open
  INS -> INS : stream-parse users-*.json\n(bounded memory, never full load)
  INS -> IX : write rows\n(+ clients, roles, groups, keys)
  note right of IX
    Holds credential PRESENCE only
    (has OTP / passkey count),
    never credential VALUES.
  end note
end
IX --> INS : matching rows + facets
INS --> UI : paginated table + user detail

== Optional — reveal a secret ==
User -> UI : Reveal client secret (explicit action)
UI -> INS : RevealSecret(ref, reason)
INS -> CV : decrypt just that field
INS -> INS : write audit entry (who/what/when)
INS --> UI : value shown, auto-hidden

== Close — the index does not outlive the session ==
User -> UI : Close snapshot
UI -> INS : Close(snapshotID)
INS -> IX : drop tables + delete SQLite file (secure_delete)
note right of IX
  Built on open, forgotten on close.
  No usernames, emails or group data
  are left on disk between sessions.
end note
INS --> UI : closed

@enduml
